title: "Open Nursing Core FHIR Implementation Guide (ONC-IG)"
version: 1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.1234567
date-released: 2026-01-27
url: "https://opennursingcoreig.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Clinical-Quality-Artifical-Intelligence/open-nursing-core-ig"
license: MIT

abstract: >
  The Open Nursing Core FHIR Implementation Guide (ONC-IG) provides foundational HL7 FHIR R4
  profiles for the nursing process (ADPIE), including structured assessments for NEWS2, MUST,
  Abbey Pain Scale, Glasgow Coma Scale, and Clinical Frailty. It includes an Equity Module
  with computable safety constraints to address documented clinical bias in skin assessment
  for patients with darker skin tones, led by Kumbi Kariwo FRCN QN.
  Aligned to PRSB Standards, NMC Standards of Proficiency (2018), and NHS clinical frameworks.
  Hosted by the United Nations International Computing Centre (UNICC).

keywords:
  - FHIR
